        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport, Santa Barbara Municipal Airport, Staunton, Augusta County, Virginia, Santa Barbara, California, Grottoes\n- Systems: IATA, ICAO, FAA LID\n- Events: Henson Airlines Flight 1517 crash\n\nFacts:\n- On September 23, 1985, Henson Airlines Flight 1517 crashed in Grottoes, Virginia, while on approach to Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport is a public airport located 10 nautical miles northeast of the central business district of Staunton in Augusta County, Virginia, United States.\n- Shenandoah Valley Regional Airport has the identifiers IATA SHD, ICAO KSHD, and FAA LID SHD.\n- Santa Barbara Municipal Airport is a public airport located 7 miles west of downtown Santa Barbara, California, United States.\n- Santa Barbara Municipal Airport has the identifiers IATA SBA, ICAO KSBA, and FAA LID SBA.",
